---
import SiteIllustration from '../../components/landing/SiteIllustration.astro';
/**
 * Simple public changelog for texuli.com (linked from the landing footer).
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { texuliPackageVersion } from '../../lib/schema.ts';

/** The current release, read from the texuli package manifest at build. */
const current = texuliPackageVersion();

const entries = [
  {
    version: '0.15',
    date: '2026-11',
    items: [
      "Blueprint spec 0.13.0, locked design systems: a design-system document gains allow (the catalog ids, Texuli's or a host extension's <ns>:<id>, with their enabled variants, sizes, tones, densities and states; up to 4096 ids), library (the design system's own components, each with its own approval) and approval (status, approvedBy, approvedAt, version and a SHA-256 contentHash). extends, variants and patches carry allow and library; approval is never inherited. Every 0.12.0 document stays valid.",
      'designSystemContentHash, approveDesignSystem, initLockedDesignSystem and checkDesignSystemAllow in @texuli/spec/design-system, and the compiler emits an allow manifest beside the CSS. An approval records who approved; it cannot prove it: a reviewed commit through CODEOWNERS is the guarantee.',
      "The agent catalog lists each component's styling axes, observable states and public imports, and grows from 170 to 194 ids (typography, display, app and input components, governed by allow; 75 stay agent-emittable). mergeCatalogs merges host catalog extensions with stable refusal codes, and every catalog component root carries data-tx-component and its axis attributes.",
      'Heading, Text, Prose and Box in texuli/typography set type and surfaces from --tx-* tokens; Button and IconButton take tone (default, destructive, success, warning), independent of variant. A link-variant Button keeps its text size (a fix before release).',
      'texuli ds init --locked, ds approve (the only door that writes an approved document), ds hash, and ds check reports the allowed set, the approval as declared and stale content hashes; ds.allow lists an allow section, and ds.save refuses an approved document. A fix before release: designSystemContentHash no longer mutates a document without approval, so library-hash-mismatch fires.',
      'In development, completed in 0.16.0: the design-system kit (texuli/ds-kit, /design-systems/kit/), texuli ds generate and the importers, the locked checkers in @texuli/tools/ds-check, portable design-system bundles (ds pack, ds unpack, ds.bundle), the contract schemas, the blueprint allow check and the Studio for locked systems.',
      'No breaking API change; a 0.x minor because of the new spec.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.14',
    date: '2026-11',
    items: [
      'TimelineView in @texuli/data/timeline groups rows under header rows through getGroup, with date bands, bind:collapsed and onCollapsedChange, onGroupAdd, bind:selectedRow and onRowSelect, and vertical markers. The agent catalog lists the groups, markers and the bindable collapsed and selectedRow on data-timeline, with a new collapse event; onGroupAdd is not in the catalog.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.12.0: a shadow layer takes an optional darkOpacity, the card content font size is a component token (components.card["font-size"], --tx-card-font-size), and the catalog gains the code-field and avatar-group-grid ids and the media-image srcDark and darkMode props. Every 0.11.0 document stays valid.',
      'Design-system compiler version 3: compiled hashes change once, and sidebarPrimary is also derived under a color.roles primary pin (an explicit sidebarPrimary pin is kept and reported). The new aa-non-text code checks role fills at 3:1 (WCAG 1.4.11): an invisible active sidebar item fails texuli ds check, ds.validate and --render.',
      'MotionLoop in texuli/motion/loop loops a pulse or a wave and stays still under reduced motion; it is not in the blueprint motion vocabulary, because a loop there could not be stopped.',
      'registerIcons takes lazy loaders with a fallback; AlertDialog takes confirmDisabled; Breadcrumb items take ariaLabel and onSelect; tabs without a rendered panel omit aria-controls and take panelId; a disabled Tooltip keeps its trigger enabled; dialog and sheet scrims read --tx-scrim, so dark scrims are dark again.',
      'No breaking API change; a 0.x minor because of the new spec and compiler version.',
      '0.14.1 (patch): CalendarView in @texuli/data/calendar/view takes an event snippet for the chip content in every view (the chip stays a button named by its visible content), and the month view takes maxEventsPerDay and onMoreEvents, which makes "3 more events" a button that opens the day; Board in @texuli/data/board takes bind:collapsedLanes with a disclosure toggle in each lane heading (a collapsed lane still counts in column totals and WIP limits) and a cellFooter(column, lane) snippet. Blueprint spec stays 0.12.0.',
      '0.14.2 (patch): a Dialog, AlertDialog or Sheet mounted open shows its backdrop; a non-modal Popover or Select keeps focus that moved to another overlay; a controlled Toggle or ToggleGroup renders its prop (with bind:pressed and onPressedChange, the handler sets the value). TimelineView in @texuli/data/timeline takes formatTick and initialDate, with compact day ticks, and opens at today when today is within the plan. ToggleGroup deselectable, Select block and a ghost trigger, Sidebar item icons, badgeLabel on sidebar and bottom-nav items, an IconButton badge, Stepper phrases in the label dictionary, new CSS hooks (toggle, radio, switch, placeholder, tabs badge, dialog close icon, PIN cell, --tx-scrim-blur), and side sheets, drawers and DetailPanel fill their block size. Blueprint spec stays 0.12.0.',
      '0.14.3 (patch): labelContent on Checkbox, Radio and Switch; a Field counter; NumberField display output; Avatar tone and shape; Button iconSize; BottomNav action items; MobileHeader eyebrow and close; SplitView list width, breakpoint and context pane; Stat tone; Composer row layout; ListItem in texuli/list-item; slide card icons from the icon registry; DeckStage canvasFit reflow; opt-in Spanish label catalogs (texuli/i18n/es, @texuli/blocks/i18n/es, @texuli/pages/i18n/es). Blueprint spec stays 0.12.0.',
      '0.14.4 (patch): TimelineView in @texuli/data/timeline holds its opening day while rows load after mount and while the zoom changes, until the reader scrolls, and exports scrollToDate(date).',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.13',
    date: '2026-11',
    items: [
      'Blueprint spec 0.11.0 extends the design-system document: elevation.levels (structured shadows for levels 1 to 5), extensions (product tokens compiled to --tx-ext-<name> and -foreground), a categorical palette of 1 to 8 colors with the rest derived, and a pinned soft foreground checked as its own pair. Every 0.10.0 document stays valid and formatVersion stays 1.',
      'Design-system compiler version 2: compiled hashes change, and the sidebar primary is derived when copying the primary pin would match the sidebar fill or fail contrast.',
      'One label dictionary (ADR-026): @texuli/core/i18n, and LabelsProvider and setTexuliLabels in texuli/i18n, translate the built-in labels of texuli, primitives, blocks and pages; a label prop still wins, then the nearest dictionary, then English. data, chat, media and editor keep their per-component labels props (planned).',
      'texuli ds check --render works in a consumer: the conformance sheet and its third-party notices ship in @texuli/tools, and a missing playwright or @axe-core/playwright gets a clear error.',
      'Chart titles rank by their section through @texuli/charts/heading, and every agent-emittable catalog example paints inside layout-page; the timeline gains data-part hooks, markerClass, per-status tone variables and a gap that accepts 0.',
      'No breaking API change; a 0.x minor because of the new spec and compiler version.',
      '0.13.1 (patch): registerIcons and IconsProvider in texuli/icons name your own icons for <Icon icon="name">; CodeField in @texuli/blocks/code-field edits syntax-highlighted code with no HTML sinks; Image in @texuli/media/image takes srcDark and darkMode and follows the Texuli theme; AvatarGroupGrid in texuli/avatar fits up to four faces in one circle. Blueprint spec stays 0.11.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.12',
    date: '2026-11',
    items: [
      'The @texuli/pages core entries validate without the deck model (G136): @texuli/pages/editor-core measures 76,670 B gzip (about 92.8 KB before) and @texuli/pages/host-core 13,478 B (about 29.5 KB before).',
      'Breaking for the core entries only: PageEditorCore, CollabEditorCore, new PagesEditor(...) and createDocumentPlayerHostCore take validateDeck with no default and refuse inline decks without it; pass checkDeckPayload from @texuli/document/schema, and use createDocumentDraftCheck(checkDeckPayload) for draft checks. PageEditor, CollabEditor and createDocumentPlayerHost behave as before.',
      'Blueprint spec stays 0.10.0; @texuli/spec 0.12.0 ships it unchanged.',
      '0.12.1 (patch): DeckStage takes coverHeadingLevel, so a deck embedded in a page titles its cover with h2 and the page keeps one h1.',
      '0.12.2 (patch): no package code change; the first release published through npm trusted publishing, and the next dist-tag stays on 0.12.1 (install the default latest).',
      '0.12.3 (patch): no package code change; it checks publishing through npm trusted publishing with every package refusing tokens.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.11',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'Lighter design-system hosts (G127): @texuli/tokens/design-system/compile-core, @texuli/player/design-system-core and loadDesignSystemCompilerCore() in texuli/design-system compile and paint a design system with no theme library in any chunk.',
      'Breaking for the core entries only: DeckStageCore, DeckPrintViewCore, PageReaderCore and createDocumentPlayerHostCore no longer load the theme library unless the host passes a loader (loadDeckLibraryTheme, loadDeckLibraryBase, loadPagesLibraryBase); the default entries behave as before.',
      'The library theme ids without the library in @texuli/tokens/library-ids (G125), and complete expand theme descriptions (G126).',
      'A design system with one mode never throws: it paints its compiled mode; the player and pages cores report design-system-refused instead of rejecting, and DesignSystemProvider calls onapplyerror.',
      'Blueprint spec stays 0.10.0; @texuli/spec 0.11.0 ships it unchanged.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.10',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'Design systems: one JSON document per brand, validated with stable codes, compiled to scoped --tx-* variables with text contrast, the focus ring and target size enforced, and applied by components, blueprints, decks, documents and every output (email, PDF, DOCX, PPTX, canvas exports, Kotlin tokens).',
      'The Design System Studio at /theme-studio/ and the /design-systems/ hub with three fictional example brands.',
      'Design system tools for agents: ds operations on the MCP and texuli ds commands, plus texuli ds check and @texuli/tools/ds-check for conformance in CI.',
      'Removed after one minor: the seven 0.8 MCP tool names and the tree block’s style key; a call or block that still uses one is refused with the replacement named.',
      'Fixes Protoyard reported (G100 to G124), with new entries for lighter hosts: @texuli/tokens/system.css, @texuli/slides/export-core, @texuli/forms/controls and the @texuli/pages core entries.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.10.0, additive (the design-system document), a stamp-only migration from 0.9.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.9',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'An MCP server for agents: remote at https://texuli.com/mcp and local with npx -y @texuli/mcp (a new package), both on one operations registry.',
      'An agent-ready texuli.com: Markdown twins of every page, discovery files, a read-only JSON API with an OpenAPI description, and a WebMCP bridge.',
      'Token contract v2: system token families, a component token tier and default variants and sizes, adopted by every styled package.',
      'Overlays keep the theme and tokens of the scope that opened them.',
      'Fixes Protoyard reported (G87 to G99): dialog and command palette callbacks, date control hooks and invalid state, keyboard rows in table grids, ref and rest on layouts, a time x-axis for charts and contained toasts without a forced layout.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.9.0, a stamp-only migration from 0.8.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.8',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'First publication of @texuli/forms, @texuli/canvas and @texuli/sheets: schema-driven forms and host data sources, the infinite canvas and spreadsheets with an owned formula engine.',
      'Dashboards in @texuli/data, multi-target output (email-safe HTML, print and PDF, one i18n message catalog) and the texuli.com feature pages.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.8.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.7',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'First publication of @texuli/document and @texuli/pages: the block document engine, its editor and reader.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.7.0: documents as agent data and node keys, with catalog, player and tools support.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.6',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'One API contract across components, motion, streamed blueprints, @texuli/core/markup and zip, and the gaps Protoyard reported on 0.5.0 (G48 to G85).',
      'Blueprint spec 0.6.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.5',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'First publication of @texuli/editor, the rich text editor, and the gaps Protoyard found adopting Texuli from npm.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.5.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.4',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'First publication of @texuli/deck; every drag surface in @texuli/data runs on @texuli/drag, and blueprints become interactive.',
      'Blueprint spec 0.4.0.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.3',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'First publication of @texuli/date, @texuli/drag and @texuli/workflows; the calendar entry fell from about 13.05 to 5.15 KiB gzip.',
    ],
  },
  {
    version: '0.2',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: ['The first non-prerelease 0.x line, for the 15 packages packable then.'],
  },
  {
    version: '0.1',
    date: '2026-10',
    items: [
      'The 0.1 previews on the next tag: 41 owned primitives (42 today) and the Texuli component layer on Svelte 5.',
      'Theme engine with a 210-theme library target, token contract and CSS apply path.',
      'Agent surfaces: catalog, safe renderer, skill pack and llms.txt.',
      'Library landing on texuli.com with live interactive moments.',
    ],
  },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Changelog"
  description={`What shipped in each Texuli release, from the 0.1 previews to ${current}: new packages, breaking changes and the blueprint spec version.`}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <SiteIllustration art="page-guides" class="page-head__art" />
    <h1>Changelog</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Every Texuli release, newest first. <code>{current}</code> is the current release on npm, pre-1.0:
      under <code>0.x</code> a new minor may break, so pin the version. Demos of each new capability
      are on <a href="/whats-new/">What’s new</a>; the full notes, with every closed gap and
      migration, are in the repository’s release document.
    </p>
  </header>

  {
    entries.map((entry) => (
      <section class="release" aria-labelledby={`v-${entry.version}`}>
        <h2 id={`v-${entry.version}`}>
          Texuli {entry.version} <span class="when">{entry.date}</span>
        </h2>
        <ul>
          {entry.items.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
    ))
  }
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-block-end: 2rem;
  }
  .page-head__art {
    max-inline-size: 40rem;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  .lead {
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: 40rem;
    color: var(--tx-muted-foreground);
  }
  .release {
    margin-block-end: 1.75rem;
  }
  .release h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }
  .when {
    color: var(--tx-muted-foreground);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-inline-start: 1.2rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-block: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
